<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ang Chan I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1566</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ang Chan I was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> in the 16th century, in the period after the abandonment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a>. He fought off Siamese invasions and moved the royal capital to Longvek, near the Tonlé Sap river, which remained the centre of the kingdom until its capture by Siam in 1594.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ang-chan-i.jpg" alt="Ang Chan I" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Radosław Botev · CC BY 3.0 pl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wat_Preah_Prom_Rath,_Siem_Reap_(6).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
